<description>&lt;p&gt;Rebel and SPLA-IO forces have continued lethal attacks, killing civilians in Tonj East and Warrap State, including 24 civilians with children and women, and 15 civilians in an armed assault in Warrap. Cattle-theft raids have turned deadly, leaving more than 20 dead, and an abduction prompted MSF to suspend all activities in Yei River County. UNMISS is supporting efforts to deter further violence in Tonj East after intercommunal clashes, while the Juba Teaching Hospital director has called for more support for poor patients and a football referee shot in the head died in Juba hospital. According to UCDP, there were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/sudan/unhcr-iom-vulnerability-profiling-dashboard-october-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://reliefweb.int/report/south-sudan/unhcr-south-sudan-population-overview-refugees-and-asylum-seekers-31-october-2026&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb (OCHA)&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Nigerian Voice&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxPUmNzOHdGN2VGVTVpN1JWR0NFbmxtM0ttNldsMEtSaGQwdGRiV0ZKQVJfdkdKQURGWGx2WDZGS1plRktZbEFXZGtfMnl2X0p0Uk1oZzlBTEtmeFFtbkhJWjFMNGY2SHA5LUl3akxWckFSdUhyWnV3RU55bTFJdjUtTGdaam5IREdPYkJmaVIwaHM4a0ZKamxRc2lfbEkwS2M3dlBMeEgtUlByMV84X28xR1M4Tm9kTkdTcDhIZTZB?oc=5&quot;&gt;Yeni Safak English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africa.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPY2dtYnh6aFIzVlUwYXljbFdYT1NZNkl4VHFISnRTR1dfTTl2RUVFbVJ2VHVUSm52T2s2aTIyd05SUENPbGNvdUM0aURTUXMxU1hKby0xYmo0MnpQcEFOTWpiVzBzTnpPeTh0YjZRaVNMM09lUTBKN3JnS25tenpaUVp4TWNJb1BDRjlrRElyRzllU25PaUV3?oc=5&quot;&g